{"id":"mimid-1wgh.100","title":"JMAP: jmap-chat-wss: WebSocket transport and ephemeral events","description":"In scope by decision mimid-1wgh.98 (Mark, 2026-11-22). Not planned: read the draft, face the tension below, and put a plan in this field for Mark before any code.

WHAT THE DRAFT DOES. RFC 8887 WebSocket for the JMAP Chat methods, plus ChatTypingEvent and ChatPresenceEvent as server-to-client messages, with a capability and two control messages for subscribing.

THE TENSION: it overlaps mimid's own live stream (docs/design/binary-live-stream.md), which is already a second binding between agent and provider behind a switch. Decide whether this replaces the live stream for standard clients, sits beside it, or is only a client-facing transport at the agent. And MIMI has no presence, so ChatPresenceEvent has nothing to carry; whether MIMI has any typing signal must be checked in mimi-content-10 before claiming support for the other.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mark@reviewcommit.com","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.167612415Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.167612415Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"mimid-1wgh.100","depends_on_id":"mimid-1wgh","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-11-22T22:47:06.198009603Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","metadata":"{}"}]}
